Package: SACAT
Type: Package
Title: Structural-Absence and Conditional-Abundance Testing
Version: 0.7.1
Authors@R:
    c(
        person("Yiqian", "Zhang", email = "zhang.16383@osu.edu",
               role = c("aut", "cre")),
        person("Zihan", "Zhu", email = "zihan.zhu@yale.edu",
               role = "aut")
    )
URL: https://github.com/yiqianomics/SACAT
BugReports: https://github.com/yiqianomics/SACAT/issues
Description: Provides depth-aware taxon-level inference for microbiome count
    data. SACAT separates group differences in structural-absence probability
    from differences in mean log relative abundance among samples in which a
    taxon is present. It accounts for finite-depth nondetection, centers
    abundance effects against a target-excluded cross-taxon reference, reports
    component-specific and omnibus tests, and provides aligned plots of fitted
    group contrasts and statistical evidence.
